WEBVTT

01:33.710 --> 01:36.460
It's not nice to keep things to yourself.

01:36.460 --> 01:39.780
Everyone should share in the fun...

01:42.210 --> 01:44.540
Revolutionary Knight Sunraku-kun.

01:45.050 --> 01:47.540
You've shown your face, Pencil Knight!

01:47.540 --> 01:48.730
Hey, now.

01:48.010 --> 01:49.900
<i>"Revolutionary Knight Sunraku."</i>

01:48.730 --> 01:50.730
Don't talk to a supreme beauty like me

01:49.900 --> 01:53.550
<i>This title has no meaning in the game of <i>SLF</i>.</i>

01:51.200 --> 01:54.290
like she's some annoying monster.

01:53.550 --> 01:55.310
<i>It's a signifier of a relationship</i>

01:55.310 --> 01:59.690
<i>between Sunraku and a certain other 
player in a certain other game.</i>

01:55.770 --> 01:57.170
Besides...

01:59.690 --> 02:02.900
in <i>SLF</i>, I'm not Pencil Knight.

02:03.450 --> 02:07.610
Kindly call me Arthur Pencilgon.

02:09.810 --> 02:12.860
<b><i>Arthur Pencilgon</i></b>

02:16.460 --> 02:20.610
<b>The Writing Tool Knight-Queen</b>

02:17.070 --> 02:20.610
My friend in trash gamerhood, 
Pencil Knight...

02:20.610 --> 02:23.620
Or should I say... Arthur Pencilgon.

02:30.600 --> 02:33.480
<i>In order to discuss her, 
we first need to talk</i>

02:33.750 --> 02:38.130
<b>Item Shop</b>

02:34.120 --> 02:37.010
<i>about a certain trash game 
known as <i>Unite Rounds</i>.</i>

02:38.130 --> 02:38.720
<b>Sales Counter</b>

02:40.990 --> 02:43.370
Take anything you want! Just don't kill me!

02:43.370 --> 02:44.910
Let's clean the place out!

02:44.910 --> 02:46.600
If he tries anything, kill him!

02:46.600 --> 02:47.600
Yeah!

02:49.160 --> 02:52.020
Hey, this guy's got quite a stash!

02:52.020 --> 02:56.530
<b>Item Shop</b>

02:53.190 --> 02:54.740
Yeah! What a haul!

02:54.740 --> 02:56.530
Now, let's split.

02:56.530 --> 02:59.860
I'm not gonna spend another 
day on my hands and knees!

03:01.130 --> 03:05.910
Sunraku

03:01.980 --> 03:04.100
Nice work getting those items!

03:04.100 --> 03:05.910
It's shakedown time.

03:08.970 --> 03:12.790
<i>The players called it a 
"Post-Apocalyptic Looting Simulator."</i>

03:13.540 --> 03:17.550
<i>The game was originally meant to simulate 
a kingdom on the verge of collapse,</i>

03:17.920 --> 03:21.720
<i>with players assuming the role of knights 
who protect it from attacking monsters—</i>

03:21.720 --> 03:24.420
<i>A co-op MMO VR game.</i>

03:28.060 --> 03:33.120
<i>But because of truly garbage design that 
prioritized faithfulness to the concept,</i>

03:33.120 --> 03:35.670
<i>the drop rate was unreasonably low,</i>

03:35.380 --> 03:37.980
<b>This rock's not even suitable
for throwing.</b>

03:35.670 --> 03:37.980
<i>and precious few players 
tried to play it "the right way."</i>

03:38.340 --> 03:41.990
Even the rocks have a 40% drop rate?!

03:41.990 --> 03:45.640
<i>Even the beginner's quest, 
"Gather Medicinal Herbs,"</i>

03:45.640 --> 03:51.000
<i>required twelve hours of combing 
through open fields to complete.</i>

03:51.210 --> 03:56.000
<i>Naturally, higher grade items 
were even harder to find.</i>

03:57.100 --> 03:58.670
<i>What were the players to do?</i>

03:59.490 --> 04:01.130
<i>The answer was simple:</i>

04:02.100 --> 04:03.540
<i>Steal what they needed.</i>

04:04.430 --> 04:05.910
<i>"Find medicinal herbs?</i>

04:05.910 --> 04:08.970
<i>You expect me to spend hours picking 
through the grass for that crap?</i>

04:08.970 --> 04:14.490
<i>I'll just raid an NPC store, 
or steal them from a player who did."</i>

04:14.490 --> 04:17.210
<i>That proved to be the winning 
move in </i>Unite Rounds<i>.</i>

04:21.290 --> 04:26.190
<i>In an environment where outrage was 
rampant and everyone was an enemy,</i>

04:26.190 --> 04:29.960
<i>a lone figure arose, 
fueled by violence and cunning,</i>

04:29.960 --> 04:32.580
<i>to take control of the kingdom.</i>

04:33.140 --> 04:34.870
<b>Pencil Knight</b>

04:35.290 --> 04:38.670
Let's all share the wealth and drop items!

04:41.170 --> 04:42.870
The kingdom is ours!

04:42.870 --> 04:44.960
Comrade Pencil Knight!

04:44.960 --> 04:47.930
Yeah! Pencil Knight!

04:47.930 --> 04:50.330
<i>And thus, the Pencil Kingdom was born.</i>

04:57.560 --> 05:09.580
Katzo Tataki

04:57.560 --> 05:09.580
Sunraku

05:10.320 --> 05:11.700
Hey, Sunraku.

05:12.070 --> 05:13.610
Yeah, Katzo?

05:14.190 --> 05:16.210
Aw, yeah, that's good stuff!

05:16.590 --> 05:20.210
Isn't this game about defending 
the kingdom from monsters?

05:20.470 --> 05:21.720
Is it?

05:21.720 --> 05:25.190
I thought it was about defeating 
the true big bad, Pencil Knight.

05:25.710 --> 05:29.850
<i>Pencil Knight was nothing like the final 
boss built into the game's story.</i>

05:30.550 --> 05:34.140
<i>She would intentionally abuse players
who she didn't allow into her ranks,</i>

05:34.140 --> 05:38.230
<i>then use her agents to create
organized resistance to oppose her.</i>

05:38.440 --> 05:41.190
<i>Thus, she fomented the will to 
fight back in her victims,</i>

05:41.190 --> 05:44.230
<i>preventing them from simply 
giving up on the game.</i>

05:45.180 --> 05:47.740
Well, shall we get to the assassination?

05:52.700 --> 05:59.080
Sunraku

05:52.720 --> 05:59.080
Katzo Tataki

05:54.100 --> 05:57.750
<i>At this time, the game of </i>Unite Rounds <i>
was completely at the whim of one player,</i>

05:59.390 --> 06:05.630
<i>acting under a name she'd picked up 
at some point—the Dystopian Empress.</i>

06:01.150 --> 06:05.630
Dystopian Empress

06:06.250 --> 06:09.130
You used the rebel army as a distraction

06:09.130 --> 06:12.140
to slip a small strike force 
into my inner chambers? Nice.

06:13.310 --> 06:16.410
You coulda set some more effective traps.

06:16.410 --> 06:19.140
They were so easy we broke 
through 'em on the first try!

06:19.520 --> 06:21.840
Sunraku-kun. Katzo Tataki-kun.

06:22.820 --> 06:23.800
I'll remember that.

06:24.980 --> 06:29.040
Something about that goofy smirk 
of yours really gets on my nerves.

06:32.010 --> 06:34.060
It's time for the boss battle.

06:32.180 --> 06:37.370
Pencil Knight

06:34.060 --> 06:37.370
Can you defeat me and become 
the Revolutionary Knight?

06:43.150 --> 06:44.630
In other words...

06:44.630 --> 06:48.030
She and I have one hell of a history.

06:48.030 --> 06:51.970
In <i>Unite Rounds</i>, we fought each other to a draw,
with both of us dying in the end.

06:51.970 --> 06:54.390
And here, we've got a big level gap in play.

07:00.240 --> 07:04.800
I took the penalty and came all 
the way from Fifticia to PK you.

07:04.800 --> 07:07.940
You must be <i>so</i> grateful and flattered! 
Feel free to cry!

07:18.390 --> 07:21.810
I'll bet those knives have 
a poison attribute, right?

07:21.810 --> 07:25.380
They're pretty expensive for 
one-use items, you know...

07:28.030 --> 07:31.390
By the way, Sunraku-kun. 
What level are you at?

07:33.090 --> 07:37.210
If you just beat Mud Digger, 
you've got to be around 30, right?

07:37.210 --> 07:39.310
That's some really impressive dodging, then.

07:39.310 --> 07:41.210
That's the god-tier game factor.

07:41.210 --> 07:43.310
All my moves come nice and smooth.

07:44.190 --> 07:46.410
Pencilgon... is she...

07:47.070 --> 07:52.030
Second in command of that player 
killer clan, Ashura Kai...

07:49.840 --> 07:54.320
<b>Ashura Kai</b>

07:52.030 --> 07:53.740
The Giant Killer?!

07:52.260 --> 07:54.320
<b>Giant Killer</b>

07:56.950 --> 07:59.910
Oh, dear! Oh, dear!

07:59.910 --> 08:02.250
"Giant Killer"?

08:02.520 --> 08:05.400
I focused on ambushing higher-level players,

08:05.400 --> 08:08.290
and at some point, 
I just picked up the nickname.

08:08.290 --> 08:12.840
But the devs nerfed how that works, 
so it's been a lot harder lately.

08:14.720 --> 08:16.630
Now, hang on a minute...

08:17.150 --> 08:21.170
In that dystopia, <i>you</i> were the 
giant who got yourself killed!

08:21.170 --> 08:24.270
Giants who live in glass houses 
shouldn't throw boulders!

08:30.750 --> 08:33.830
That's a clever turn of phrase 
for a birdbrain like you!

08:33.830 --> 08:36.020
You been studying hard lately, huh?

08:37.280 --> 08:39.300
And don't you talk about that here!

08:39.300 --> 08:41.480
I've got a bird <i>head</i>, not a bird <i>brain</i>!

08:41.480 --> 08:43.100
You moron!

08:45.290 --> 08:48.220
Wh-What's with those two?

08:49.300 --> 08:53.510
Matter of fact, I didn't <i>just </i>
come here for personal reasons!

08:55.510 --> 09:00.010
The leader of my clan, Ashura Kai, 
asked me to deliver a message!

09:00.010 --> 09:01.350
A message?!

09:02.180 --> 09:05.020
"Publish info on the unique scenario,

09:05.020 --> 09:08.380
or wear a target on your back until you do!"

09:08.770 --> 09:11.280
He's threatening <i>me</i>?!

09:21.380 --> 09:23.080
Sounds like a real dumbass.

09:24.160 --> 09:25.400
Oh, he is.

09:37.850 --> 09:39.420
<i>Still, what do I do here?</i>

09:39.420 --> 09:42.430
<i>There's too big a gap in 
our equipment and levels.</i>

09:44.970 --> 09:49.560
Still, seems like you're trying hard 
to keep me away from that gate.

09:49.560 --> 09:55.820
I'll bet you timed that first attack to 
prevent me from entering the city, too.

09:55.820 --> 10:01.410
Is it that hard for a player killer to do 
their thing in a highly populated town?

10:02.330 --> 10:05.950
Well... I'd certainly prefer 
to avoid it if I can.

10:08.210 --> 10:11.580
Besides, you're <i>not</i> making 
it to the gate, are you?

10:19.000 --> 10:20.330
My tail!

10:20.330 --> 10:24.100
<i>Sunraku-san, I can't hold it any longer!</i>

10:24.350 --> 10:27.670
<i>I'm going to lose my transformed state!</i>

10:31.180 --> 10:35.730
<i>Darn it! I found him first!</i>

10:35.730 --> 10:39.340
<i>But... he's fighting the 
infamous Giant Killer...</i>

10:39.750 --> 10:41.960
<i>Oh, wait! I can ask his companion...</i>

10:46.040 --> 10:50.630
<i>Eh? Was she always wearing 
those tail and ear accessories?</i>

10:51.370 --> 10:53.000
Hey, can I ask you—

10:56.490 --> 10:58.550
Wh-What the...

11:13.330 --> 11:14.360
Emul!

11:15.280 --> 11:16.950
<i>At the worst possible moment!</i>

11:21.200 --> 11:23.570
P-Please, calm yourself!

11:24.650 --> 11:25.770
That's it!

11:26.540 --> 11:28.540
Getting distracted? I'm not 
enough of an opponent for you?

11:30.710 --> 11:32.000
Yeah, right!

11:33.000 --> 11:35.000
<b>Repel Counter</b>

11:37.380 --> 11:41.140
<i>You're</i> the one going easy on <i>me</i>!

11:44.010 --> 11:46.260
Figured it out, did you?

11:46.750 --> 11:48.140
Emul! C'mere!

11:50.760 --> 11:51.390
On my way!

11:56.150 --> 11:57.380
W-Wait!

11:57.380 --> 12:00.150
At least let me get a screenshot with her!

12:00.440 --> 12:03.620
If we survive this, I'll think about it!

12:04.410 --> 12:05.550
"Survive"?

12:10.640 --> 12:14.040
You're not fast enough to get away from me.

12:27.840 --> 12:30.310
I don't give a damn about that player...

12:30.700 --> 12:33.900
But if you're gonna put that 
sweet little bunny in danger...

12:34.390 --> 12:38.320
I'll slay you where you stand, Giant Killer!

12:39.150 --> 12:40.860
<i>Yes, nice one!</i>

12:40.860 --> 12:42.760
<i>I got her to put herself 
in harm's way for me!</i>

12:42.760 --> 12:44.630
<i>Animalia, was it?</i>

12:44.630 --> 12:47.660
<i>I could tell she was 
pretty hung up on Emul...</i>

12:48.050 --> 12:52.160
Boy, you make a great mascot, too, Emul!

12:53.190 --> 12:57.570
<i>Now I just need to get into town and have 
her make me a teleport gate to Rabituza!</i>

12:57.570 --> 12:59.920
<i>No one should be able to track me there!</i>

13:05.850 --> 13:08.970
I'm the only one serving as <i>messenger</i>...

13:11.390 --> 13:16.390
<b><i>Remy</i></b>

13:11.390 --> 13:16.390
<b><i>Branch</i></b>

13:11.390 --> 13:16.390
<b><i>Lass</i></b>

13:11.390 --> 13:16.390
<b><i>Ketchum</i></b>

13:11.730 --> 13:16.390
But I never said I came here alone.

13:16.390 --> 13:22.780
<b><i>Ketchum</i></b>

13:16.390 --> 13:22.780
Man, I hate PKing low-level scrubs. 
It's hell on your karma points.

13:22.780 --> 13:25.200
<b><i>Lass</i></b>

13:22.780 --> 13:25.200
Our bosses feel the same way.

13:25.200 --> 13:28.820
<b><i>Branch</i></b>

13:25.200 --> 13:28.820
That's why they send us 
to do their dirty work.

13:28.820 --> 13:32.540
<b><i>Remy</i></b>

13:29.080 --> 13:30.420
Stop complaining.

13:30.420 --> 13:32.540
You wanna get PKed by Pencilgon-san?

13:32.540 --> 13:35.830
<b><i>Ketchum</i></b>

13:32.540 --> 13:35.830
A wild player killer appears, huh?!

13:36.250 --> 13:38.560
You're going this far 
against a low-level player?

13:40.300 --> 13:43.990
Well, delegation <i>is</i> my usual MO...

13:43.990 --> 13:48.500
Still, now I get to fight 
the keeper of SF-Zoo,

13:48.500 --> 13:51.760
a monster documenter clan with 
no interest in other players?

13:51.760 --> 13:54.380
I've really got to thank you, Sunraku-kun!

13:58.020 --> 13:59.130
Damn it!

13:59.600 --> 14:02.690
This god-tier game doesn't 
need a trash game arc!

14:07.930 --> 14:11.370
I'm gonna make you cough up that info!

14:13.430 --> 14:15.200
Four PKers.

14:15.200 --> 14:16.750
Bring it on!

14:17.050 --> 14:20.420
I mean, you've only got me beat 
in level, equipment, and stats!

14:24.420 --> 14:28.170
Take... this!

15:00.980 --> 15:02.000
<b>Poison   Paralysis      Drain    Exhaustion    Speed</b>

15:02.000 --> 15:08.010
<b>Poison   Paralysis      Drain      Exhaustion      Speed</b>

15:02.300 --> 15:03.840
Wow!

15:03.840 --> 15:08.010
You work hard on your shaman debuffs to 
help you record monster footage, right?

15:08.010 --> 15:10.340
Debuffs = Status Ailments

15:08.290 --> 15:10.340
Look at all those status ailments!

15:11.110 --> 15:14.940
You reflected all my curses?

15:14.940 --> 15:15.850
How?!

15:16.160 --> 15:20.530
There was this shaman PK killer who 
would just <i>not</i> leave me alone...

15:20.530 --> 15:23.200
So I know how scary curses can be.

15:23.200 --> 15:25.860
That's why I carry this around, just in case.

15:25.860 --> 15:29.870
A Karmic Straw Doll?!

15:28.300 --> 15:30.740
<b>Karmic Straw Doll
</b>Consumable item.
Crush it in your hand to send all curses applied
to you back at their caster. 
Attempting to expose the "something"
at the straw doll's core will kill you instantly.

15:30.740 --> 15:33.530
Counters all curses with karmic retribution!

15:33.530 --> 15:36.330
I'd have really been in trouble without it.

15:37.170 --> 15:39.370
Sorry about the rotten luck.

15:39.680 --> 15:43.250
Don't worry. I'll stick around to 
watch you die of your own poison.

15:58.060 --> 16:02.240
<i>My best target is that jerk 
who thinks I'm a scrub.</i>

16:02.240 --> 16:04.730
<i>With a slow weapon like that longsword,</i>

16:04.730 --> 16:06.270
<i>I don't even need skills 
to dodge his attacks.</i>

16:07.050 --> 16:10.370
<i>The real question is, how do 
I damage high-level players</i>

16:10.370 --> 16:12.650
<i>decked out in top-tier armor?</i>

16:13.280 --> 16:16.410
Severing attack! Rook-smasher!

16:16.660 --> 16:19.410
<b>Severing
attack,
"Rook-
smasher"</b>

16:23.940 --> 16:26.420
Wh-What in the world?!

16:28.630 --> 16:30.270
A one-hit kill?!

16:30.270 --> 16:32.720
Hang on a minute. Is that...

16:33.260 --> 16:37.070
The unparalleled firepower 
of the Attack Master?!

16:38.640 --> 16:41.800
"Attack Master"? What the hell is that?

16:42.560 --> 16:45.190
As if I didn't have enough problems here!

16:46.490 --> 16:48.260
A bird head mask.

16:48.260 --> 16:50.730
Character name: Sunraku.

16:52.530 --> 16:53.820
At last...

16:55.050 --> 16:57.570
At last I've found you,

16:58.030 --> 16:59.210
Hizutome-kun!

17:07.420 --> 17:11.690
<b>Constant Progress</b>

17:17.430 --> 17:19.070
Hizutome-kun.

17:19.580 --> 17:21.610
Where could he be?

17:22.870 --> 17:24.710
You still haven't found him?

17:27.400 --> 17:31.890
Well, you said he always plays as "Sunraku,"

17:31.890 --> 17:35.060
so I've been looking for 
him under that name...

17:35.060 --> 17:39.490
But he seems to have skipped the 
first tutorial city entirely...

17:39.820 --> 17:42.550
I'm sure you'll find him soon.

17:42.550 --> 17:44.750
Keep going, Rei-chan!

17:45.310 --> 17:46.570
Okay...

17:46.570 --> 17:48.270
Then tell him how you feel.

17:56.650 --> 18:00.840
I still can't find him anywhere, Mana-san!

18:07.490 --> 18:11.940
<i>The games he likes are so... like...</i>

18:11.940 --> 18:18.950
<b>Frog Swimmer</b>

18:11.940 --> 18:18.950
<b>Battle Circuit</b>

18:11.940 --> 18:18.950
Panty Flash Panic

18:12.450 --> 18:14.980
<i>So unusual and difficult.</i>

18:15.450 --> 18:18.310
<i>They're all too hard for me.</i>

18:19.170 --> 18:23.810
<i>I could never find a game 
that I could play with him.</i>

18:24.890 --> 18:27.250
<i>But with </i>SLF<i>...</i>

18:28.970 --> 18:31.770
<i>We've got Hizutome-kun playing it.</i>

18:32.090 --> 18:35.470
<i>I won't let this chance get away!</i>

18:47.310 --> 18:49.310
<b>You've received
a mailbird from
Psyger-100</b>

18:49.310 --> 18:51.810
Secondale  Inn

18:50.580 --> 18:51.670
Mail?

18:52.950 --> 18:54.330
From my sister?

18:57.150 --> 19:00.110
From: Psyger-100
Dear Psyger-0,
 Sorry, but I need you to pause
your private player hunt.
There's a player I really need to talk to.
Can you find him for me?

 He was last sighted near Secondale.
He seems to have a talking,
clothed Vorpal Bunny with him.

18:58.650 --> 18:59.420
What?!

19:06.670 --> 19:07.620
<i>Dear Psyger-0,</i>

19:08.590 --> 19:11.600
<i>Sorry, but I need you to pause 
your private player hunt.</i>

19:12.170 --> 19:15.000
<i>There's a player I really need to talk to.</i>

19:15.000 --> 19:17.350
<i>Can you find him for me?</i>

19:17.350 --> 19:19.430
This seems really bad.

19:19.430 --> 19:21.460
They said taking pictures 
is against the rules...

19:21.870 --> 19:24.550
I guess I should probably delete it, right?

19:25.660 --> 19:27.680
<i>He was last sighted near Secondale.</i>

19:28.010 --> 19:31.290
<i>He seems to have a talking, 
clothed Vorpal Bunny with him.</i>

19:31.840 --> 19:35.630
<i>He might already be en route to Thirdrema.</i>

19:36.490 --> 19:38.440
<i>I've attached a picture with him in it.</i>

19:38.440 --> 19:46.280
75: Alinoiyu (Beginner)
I have a question for our esteemed elders. I was picking up equipment
in Secondale when I ran into this player. He had the cutest talking bunny
with him. How can I befriend this monster?

19:39.210 --> 19:41.300
<i>He's equipped with a Staring Bird Mask,</i>

19:41.300 --> 19:44.000
<i>and his legs and torso bear Lycagon's Mark.</i>

19:44.410 --> 19:45.850
<i>His name is...</i>

19:46.490 --> 19:47.850
Sunraku.

20:02.650 --> 20:07.270
<i>A number of clans are already 
arranging to make contact with him.</i>

20:07.660 --> 20:10.670
<i>Ashura Kai is among them.</i>

20:12.310 --> 20:13.490
I found you.

20:15.090 --> 20:18.300
<i>There's a very good chance 
he's already engaged in PvP.</i>

20:15.440 --> 20:20.440
PvP = Battle between players

20:19.170 --> 20:20.440
<i>Be careful.</i>

20:20.440 --> 20:23.800
I won't get a chance like this again!

20:23.800 --> 20:29.240
If I can save him from PKers, 
I'll have a natural "in" to talk to him!

20:30.250 --> 20:31.920
Then some day...

20:32.450 --> 20:35.210
I'll be able to talk to him IRL, too!

20:43.550 --> 20:46.390
Severing attack! Rook-smasher!

20:49.360 --> 20:51.910
<i>Things are getting intense over there, too.</i>

20:51.910 --> 20:56.270
<i>Though, those PKers may not 
be able to beat Sunraku-kun...</i>

21:00.280 --> 21:03.110
<i>Fighting him in </i>SLF<i> has 
made it even more clear...</i>

21:03.930 --> 21:09.300
<i>The skills he's built up playing 
terrible games in all genres</i>

21:09.650 --> 21:13.860
<i>are more valuable than unique 
items and high-level stats.</i>

21:13.860 --> 21:18.690
<i>And that's a huge asset here 
in <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>.</i>

21:20.090 --> 21:23.180
<i>I hear Katzo-kun's playing </i>SLF<i>, as well.</i>

21:23.180 --> 21:25.130
<i>So with Sunraku-kun...</i>

21:26.170 --> 21:28.530
<i>That project of mine is 
looking more possible.</i>

21:31.950 --> 21:33.270
<i>Is that...</i>

21:33.920 --> 21:35.280
<i>Psyger-0?!</i>

21:37.760 --> 21:41.520
<i>First he lured in the Zookeeper, 
now the Attack Master?!</i>

21:41.740 --> 21:45.900
I'm so glad I came to see you, Sunraku-kun!

21:46.370 --> 21:48.730
I hit you with five spells.

21:52.160 --> 21:56.970
"Karmic Straw Doll" is extremely powerful,

21:57.550 --> 22:03.090
so each doll tops out at 
reflecting five debuffs.

22:06.510 --> 22:10.150
Can you counter my final hand?!

23:41.940 --> 23:49.200
<b>SLF Mini</b>

23:42.660 --> 23:46.460
<i><i>SLF</i></i> Theater!

23:45.750 --> 23:49.190
<i><b>Is the Food Bad in <i>SLF</i>?</b></i>

23:46.460 --> 23:47.910
Mini!

23:49.190 --> 25:16.280
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

23:51.700 --> 23:53.770
Oh, how I love carrots!

23:53.770 --> 23:57.500
They are truly the greatest of foods!

23:57.500 --> 24:00.470
The taste, the texture, the shape, the color!

24:00.470 --> 24:03.640
There has never been a food 
more perfect than the carrot!

24:03.640 --> 24:05.730
Don't you agree, Sunraku-sa—

24:08.210 --> 24:09.680
S-Sunraku-san?

24:09.680 --> 24:11.620
Are you eating <i>all</i> of those?!

24:11.620 --> 24:12.470
Yeah.

24:13.170 --> 24:15.880
Apparently, there're flavor 
limiters in this game.

24:15.880 --> 24:18.260
Flavor limiters?

24:18.610 --> 24:22.900
It might not make sense 
to an NPC like you, but...

24:22.900 --> 24:25.420
Let's say there're limiters 
on pioneers' tongues,

24:25.420 --> 24:29.850
so anything we eat just tastes 
vaguely sweet, spicy, or whatever.

24:29.850 --> 24:35.040
But I heard you can remove flavor 
limiters if you eat a ton of food.

24:37.120 --> 24:38.740
I see.

24:38.740 --> 24:41.290
But I do hope you don't gorge yourself...

24:41.540 --> 24:43.000
<i>That's weird.</i>

24:43.000 --> 24:45.360
<i>The flavor's doesn't change, 
no matter how much I eat.</i>

24:46.230 --> 24:49.970
I brought this one special 
from the Palace of Rabituza!

24:52.800 --> 24:56.120
Boy, I wish I could enjoy food that much...

25:07.690 --> 25:10.360
One level of flavor
limiter has been removed.

25:11.670 --> 25:16.280
<b>Flavor limiters are removed
through consumption of high-quality food items.</b>
